@details
1 | description |
  Check that handoff/mod.rs and other files to be deleted are not referenced elsewhere in the codebase. Perform a search for dependencies and ensure no active usage exists. Document any findings for confirmation before proceeding.
2 | description |
  Delete swarm_executor.rs, swarm_tui.rs, context_handoff.rs, and the handoff/ directory as specified. Ensure all references are cleaned up to avoid build errors.
3 | description |
  Remove re-exports for SwarmExecutor, SwarmTui, and context_handoff from lib.rs. Verify the library compiles after changes.
4 | description |
  Remove the --no-use-scud flag, SwarmExecutor fallback path, and related instantiations from main.rs, keeping only the SCUD delegation logic.
5 | description |
  Run cargo build --release and cargo test to ensure the codebase is functional post-removal. Address any compilation errors or failing tests.
6 | description |
  Plan the ScudBridge module including ScudEvent and ScudCommand enums, subprocess communication, and integration with Iced's event system. Output a design document with API signatures and data flow diagrams. Do not create initial module structure - that belongs in task 7.
7 | description |
  Code the ScudBridge struct with async methods for loading tasks, running swarms, and event streaming. Integrate JSON parsing for SCUD output and connect to the GUI's message system.
7.1 | description |
  Code the ScudBridge struct with async methods for loading tasks, running swarms, and event streaming. Include JSON parsing for SCUD output.
7.2 | description |
  Connect the ScudBridge module to the GUI's message system for event handling and communication.
8 | description |
  Refactor view_waves() and view_output() to use ScudBridge for real data loading and output streaming. Update the Message enum for new SCUD events. Note: agents view, settings view, and SCUD task management view require separate tasks per PRD Phase 3.
8.1 | description |
  Modify the Message enum to include new messages required for SCUD integration, such as those for real data loading, task management, and output streaming via ScudBridge.
8.2 | description |
  Update view_waves(), view_output(), and other GUI components to integrate ScudBridge for real data loading, task management, and output streaming, ensuring they utilize the updated Message enum.
9 | description |
  Add codebase context injection, dependency context (including outputs from completed tasks), verification commands, and a per-project template system to spec.rs. Update the guidance writer to produce richer .scud/guidance/ files.
9.1 | description |
  Add codebase context injection, dependency context, verification commands, and a template system to spec.rs. This includes defining the necessary structures and logic for these features.
9.2 | description |
  Integrate the new features into the spec generation flow to produce richer guidance files, ensuring all added contexts and commands are utilized effectively.
10 | description |
  Work with the SCUD repo to plan and track --json and --json-events flag additions. This is coordination work; actual implementation and testing are in subtasks 10.1 and 10.2.
10.1 | description |
  Add --json flag for outputting task listings in JSON format and --json-events flag for streaming events in JSON format to the SCUD CLI.
10.2 | description |
  Document the JSON event format produced by --json-events flag and test compatibility of both new flags with the GUI.
